WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:01.640
It is the period of warring states.{these top three lines were from previous ep and should not be changed or edited}{line taken from Sage's sub}

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:03.690
The era of competing warlords.{line taken from Sage's sub}

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:10.950
Many of these daimyou clashed blades ruthlessly,
aiming for conquest of the country.{line taken from Sage's sub}

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:15.490
Fate, once set in motion,
can be stopped by no one.

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:19.370
...if we continue along this course,
we will be entering Ueda, where Sanada is!

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:22.330
So I'll just have to kick aside
any pebbles that get in my way!

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:26.750
The Takeda wants an alliance
with you, Great Malevolence.

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:28.670
Fate set in motion...

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:33.300
Ishida Mitsunari!

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:38.010
It will all lead up to Sekigahara.{line taken from Sage's sub}

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:55.570
<b>It is almost two point
five decades since I was born</b>

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:57.950
<b>I've had so many of jellos so far</b>

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:00.740
<b>and how many more will I swallow from now on?</b>

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:04.210
<b>I've already taken tons of exams</b>

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:06.670
<b>and what else is coming up to me from now on?</b>

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:09.840
<b>Daily lives must pass by quickly
without any "likes'' and "hates"</b>

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:11.500
<b>That girl who falls for guys easily,</b>

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:13.970
<b>fell for another one then another
one and another one each time</b>

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:15.380
<b>For a guy without such experience</b>

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:19.640
<b>Everyday life now is like a stormy river</b>

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:20.850
<b>So fast!</b>

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:25.140
<b>Break out!</b>

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:33.530
<b>(so) I sing to myself before I get sunk</b>

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:38.410
<b>I jumped out to stop the streaming days</b>

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:44.950
<b>The coastline I ran on that strong sunny day
(Shore line I ran)</b>

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:49.630
<b>If you wanna take back that feeling
(take back that feeling)</b>

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:53.880
<b>That feeling and give it a deep color of your own self
(take back that feeling)</b>

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:56.800
<b>First, smash down that door</b>

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.190
UEDA

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.190
CASTLE

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:10.990
Who are you?

00:02:10.990 --> 00:02:12.280
Wha...?!

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:16.030
Bastard...

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:18.990
What happened at Odawara...

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:19.870
Odawara?

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:21.000
That's right!

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.710
I'm the man who fought you that day!

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:25.420
That day...

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:29.880
Be gone. Your presence offends me.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:34.090
Ishida!

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:39.560
Move aside, Sanada!

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:40.640
I will not!

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:43.180
Master Ishida is a man who
is to become my sworn friend!

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:45.650
By no means will I permit you to injure him!

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:47.020
Is that right?

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:48.270
Then...

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:51.860
I'll start by killing you first!

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:59.830
Defeat

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:10.460
This coldly hollow way of fighting...

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:12.920
This is not like you!

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:18.680
There's nothing to be like or not
be like when it's kill or be killed!

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:22.560
That desire to kill...

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:23.680
Lord Date...

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:24.810
Don't.

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:28.060
This is a fight that two generals
have chosen for themselves.

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:29.690
A fight they chose?

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:33.190
So the defeat at Odawara's clouded
the Right Eye of the Dragon, too?

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:34.570
Wha...?

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:42.200
Worthless. You think
you've stopped me with this?

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:02.390
Disgraceful.

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:04.850
Ishida!

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:08.600
<i>I</i> am your opponent!

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:13.070
W-Wait, we haven't talked
about our alliance yet.

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:14.690
As Gyobu suggested,

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:18.200
I met with the commander of
the Takeda and proposed an alliance.

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:20.870
I will hear your reply at
Lord Hideyoshi's castle.

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:23.950
Wait, Ishida! Ishida!

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:25.450
Move aside, Sanada!

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:26.370
I cannot!

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:29.210
Though it cost me my life, I will not give way!

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:32.340
Then I'll kill you, just like you want!

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:38.130
Lord Masamune...

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:44.600
<i>(Flare Storm)</i>

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:44.600
Rekka!

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:43.300
Rekka

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:43.300
Rekka

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:43.350
Rekka

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:43.350
Rekka

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:43.390
Rekka

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:43.390
Rekka

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:43.430
Rekka

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:43.430
Rekka

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:43.470
Rekka

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:43.470
Rekka

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:45.430
Rekka

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:45.430
Rekka

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:52.150
Not good! His wounds have reopened!

00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:58.440
Ishida!

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:01.240
Lord Masamune!

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:01.240
Damn.

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:03.570
Magnum Strike!

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.330
Commander!

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:23.140
Die.

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:25.680
I-I won't let you.

00:05:32.270 --> 00:05:35.190
That is far enough, Lord Masamune.

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:37.020
Let go, Kojuro!

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:39.900
These blades haven't reached Ishida yet!

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:41.200
This must not be!

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:43.110
Take a good look.

00:05:57.210 --> 00:06:00.260
I'm done with you, Sanada.

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:08.470
Lord Masamune...

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:18.980
Lord Masamune,

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:22.490
let us return to Oshu for a
time and rethink our strategy.

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:25.820
Kojuro, my answer is "no."

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:33.330
Lord Masamune, how does this
world appear through your eyes?

00:06:33.790 --> 00:06:35.540
OSAKA  CASTLE{changed this font to look more more agressive like the sign}

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:36.540
<i>Around the same time, at Osaka Castle,</i>

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:41.800
<i>Otani Yoshitsugu was charging
Chosokabe Motochika with a mission.</i>

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:43.750
As you know, we have come together

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:50.850
to stop Tokugawa's brutality
as he plots to usurp this country.

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:54.100
But may the heavens have mercy,
he is moving quick.

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:56.060
Quit beating around the bush.

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:57.690
What do we need to do?

00:06:57.690 --> 00:07:00.270
In that case, would you
be willing to do me a favor?

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:03.150
It would mean making your
way to Kyushu in the far south.

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:04.820
Kyushu?

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:07.280
We need pieces on the board.

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:09.530
Shimazu and Kuroda.

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:11.290
Otomo is another story,

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:14.750
but Tachibana, his retainer,
should prove useful.

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:18.710
If Tokugawa should ever take Kyushu,

00:07:18.710 --> 00:07:23.130
it would mean that we
would be pinned down in Osaka.

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:27.130
In other words, go win over the
rest of the folks in the west, right?

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:28.470
Leave it to me.

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:33.270
That said, it will be arduous
for you to go see them all yourself.

00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:35.020
Therefore,

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:38.350
work with Mori to see that this gets done.

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:40.020
Mori?!

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:42.820
I've gone at it with him
a hell of a lot in the past,

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:45.740
but he ain't the sort of son-of-a-bitch
that you can make nice with!

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:47.910
That's a deal breaker for me!

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:50.530
Time will not wait for us.

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:53.990
This, too, is for the sake
of bringing down Tokugawa.

00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:58.000
Aki

00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:58.790
<i>Aki.</i>

00:07:58.790 --> 00:08:02.380
<i>It is the stronghold of Mori Motonari,
who rules the western end of Honshu,</i>

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:06.090
<i>and also the largest harbor
facing the Inland Sea of Seto.</i>

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:15.890
So, it is you, Chosokabe.

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:18.230
That face of yours is
the last thing I want to see,

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:20.400
but the mess in this harbor...

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:21.810
Something happen here?

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:25.230
I have heard of the grief
that befell Shikoku recently.

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:27.450
The architect of which is Tokugawa Ieyasu,

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:29.410
who schemes to seize the country.

00:08:29.410 --> 00:08:32.490
My land was no exception
and we suffered a sneak attack.

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:34.620
Ieyasu came here, too?

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:36.200
So what brings you here?

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:38.910
Come to use this opportunity
to take Aki by storm?

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:39.920
Nah...

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:43.290
I'll settle things with you
<i>after</i> I've crushed Ieyasu!

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:46.050
Otani asked me to come here.

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:49.260
I see, so you have joined
forces with Ishida as well.

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:51.180
What did that man say?

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:56.020
He said to work with you to
get the folks in Kyushu on board.

00:08:56.020 --> 00:08:59.640
Kuroda, Shimazu, and Otomo, I suppose?

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:03.980
I'll take care of Kuroda and Shimazu.
I'll leave Otomo to you.

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:06.690
Otomo... Sorin?

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:09.700
Well, as long as we're cooperating,
I'm borrowing one of your ships.

00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:13.280
I'll be modifying it a bit pirate-style, though.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:21.460
People sure do change...

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:22.750
Ieyasu...

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:25.710
Owari

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:26.170
<i>Around the same time,</i>

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:30.090
<i>Tokugawa Ieyasu was paying
a visit to the land of Owari.</i>

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:32.340
<i>Owari had once enjoyed the utmost prosperity,</i>

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:34.800
<i>but it fell into ruin with the
decline of the house of Oda.</i>

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:36.850
<i>And now, all that remained
was the burnt husk of the castle</i>

00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:40.940
<i>which sheltered the remnants of
the Oda who managed to escape.</i>

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:44.270
Do you mean to threaten us
with Lady O-Ichi as your hostage?!

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:47.150
I would never threaten you folk.

00:09:47.150 --> 00:09:49.570
Lady O-Ichi is at the castle in Sunpu.

00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:52.990
Will you, of the house of Oda,
not join us in moving forward as well?

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:55.160
First, you switched allegiance
from the Oda to the Toyotomi

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:58.200
and now, you mean to rule the country yourself?

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:01.710
Return Lady O-Ichi to us first
and offer up the country to the Oda!

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:03.620
<i>That</i> should be your rightful course of action!

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:05.080
As to that...

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:06.250
You traitor!

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:08.250
Give Lady O-Ichi back!

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:12.880
<i>In the meantime,</i>

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:16.640
<i>working to serve Saika Magoichi,
Tsuruhime was searching for Ieyasu</i>

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:19.140
<i>and she had entered Odawara as well, but...</i>

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:20.220
Honestly!

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:22.890
I am supposed to have a fateful
encounter in the deep dark woods.

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:25.230
That was what my divinations said.

00:10:25.230 --> 00:10:26.730
Sorry we turned out to be bandits.

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:28.520
Hey!

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:30.190
Ieyasu?!

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:34.820
How dare you waylay a helpless young maiden!

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:37.240
And you once called yourselves warriors?!

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:38.660
Who the hell is this old geezer?

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:41.160
E-Elderly Sir, are you the
one I am destined to meet?

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:44.080
Not to worry. You just leave things here to me.

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:47.840
With this spear of glory,
a Hojo family heirloom...

00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:51.510
Elderly Sir...

00:10:51.510 --> 00:10:53.760
I-I am so sorry, little missy...

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:55.220
H-Hey!

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:58.260
He took care of things for us!

00:10:58.260 --> 00:10:59.560
What should I do?

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:00.930
Oh!

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:03.270
That is...

00:11:09.150 --> 00:11:10.730
Y-You are...

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:12.610
Who the hell are you?!

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:18.910
What the...?

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:24.330
Oof...

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:28.380
<i>From the gloaming, he gallantly appears</i>

00:11:28.380 --> 00:11:31.300
<i>and like a dancing feather, he saves me!</i>

00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:35.300
<i>Truly! You are the one I was destined to meet!</i>

00:11:38.180 --> 00:11:40.140
Huh?

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:43.140
Where in the world... did he go?

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:44.520
Seeing the dilapidated villages

00:11:44.520 --> 00:11:47.270
and these men, who no
longer have a place to call home,

00:11:47.270 --> 00:11:51.730
it is clear that we have not a moment
to lose in ending this time of war.

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:53.570
Oh, Ieyasu!

00:11:53.570 --> 00:11:56.820
You are... the Lady Shrine Maiden
of the Kouno of Iyo!

00:11:56.820 --> 00:11:58.280
What are you doing here?

00:11:58.280 --> 00:12:00.870
I came because I had questions for you.

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:03.490
Ask me whatever you wish.

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:05.750
Then I will not hold back.

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:09.830
What was your intention in trying
to recruit my dear lady Magoichi?

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:13.300
Do you mean to make her fight on
the frontlines, as might be expected?

00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:15.590
Are you sure you have not kidnapped anyone?

00:12:15.590 --> 00:12:18.880
In short, are you a good person?!

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:20.430
Or are you a bad person?!

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:24.100
Would you mind asking
the questions one at a time?

00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:25.720
This is too much trouble!

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:27.600
I will put the questions to your future!

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:28.980
Prithee heed me!

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:30.690
Take that!

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:56.670
That should be enough.

00:13:01.390 --> 00:13:03.050
Ieyasu...

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:06.770
What in the world are you trying to do?

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:26.200
Looks like you're finally awake, Commander.

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:29.000
Wh-What of Lord Masamune?

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:30.370
No idea.

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:33.790
To think Master Katakura saved my life...

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:37.500
I'm sure they've got a lot of
their own problems to sort out.

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:39.420
Wh-What of Lord Ishida?

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:41.220
He went back to Osaka.

00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:42.430
I see.

00:13:42.430 --> 00:13:45.050
I presented him with
quite the disgraceful sight...

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:48.720
But the Lord Masamune that I saw...

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:53.440
It was utterly unlike our past
fights that put fire in my heart.

00:13:53.440 --> 00:13:56.480
Before, you two probably related to each other

00:13:56.480 --> 00:13:59.610
as warriors who shared a
mutual respect for one another.

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:03.240
But this time, Lord Date
was just a man out for revenge

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:05.620
and you can't even fill your own
shoes as the commander of an army.

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:07.160
A man only halfway fledged.

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:10.700
A man only halfway fledged,
who cannot command his own army...

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:13.000
It is true.

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:13.960
<i>In the meantime,</i>

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:16.380
<i>it was thought that Date Masamune
was headed for Osaka Castle</i>

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:19.250
<i>in pursuit of Ishida Mitsunari. However...</i>

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:20.510
Lord Masamune,

00:14:20.510 --> 00:14:23.470
it is reckless to continue
on to Osaka Castle from here.

00:14:23.470 --> 00:14:25.840
Please reconsider.

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:28.100
Who said anything about going after Ishida?

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:30.270
We're headed for Sunpu!

00:14:30.270 --> 00:14:31.230
Wha...?!

00:14:31.230 --> 00:14:33.940
All any of those bastards
can talk about is Ieyasu.

00:14:33.940 --> 00:14:35.440
In that case, I'll crush Ieyasu

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:38.360
and force their attention towards me,
whether they like it or not!

00:14:38.360 --> 00:14:40.940
Do you seriously intend to fight with Tokugawa?

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:42.280
Exactly!

00:14:42.280 --> 00:14:44.860
You keep your nose out of it.

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:48.120
As the injured Right Eye,
you just shut up and watch.

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:53.750
Satsuma

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:54.870
<i>Around the same time, having been
tasked with bringing Kyushu on board,</i>

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:59.880
<i>Chosokabe Motochika was paying a visit
to Shimazu Yoshihiro, the ruler of Satsuma.</i>

00:15:01.260 --> 00:15:04.220
I reckoned someone'd be comin' to see me,

00:15:04.220 --> 00:15:07.050
but color me surprised that
it's the Ogre o' the Western Sea.

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:10.180
You're known as Ogre Shimazu
and then there's me...

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:12.640
Who's the one worthy of being the Ogre?!

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:17.190
To start hackin' away e'en 'fore ya
asked me whatcha came 'ere to ask!

00:15:17.190 --> 00:15:20.110
This is the best way to talk to you, right?!

00:15:20.110 --> 00:15:23.030
How about it? Would you consider
joining the western forces?

00:15:23.030 --> 00:15:26.280
The Ogre o' the Western Sea's
an interestin' man.

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:33.160
What sorta man's Ishida that a man
as formidable as ya'd follow 'im?

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:36.000
The son-of-a-bitch is honest to a fault!

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:41.170
He wants to beat that Ieyasu
bastard to a pulp, just like me!

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:42.630
Oh-ho?

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:47.010
All the sons-of-bitches
with Ishida are like that!

00:15:47.010 --> 00:15:50.760
I hear even Sanada Yukimura
of the Takeda's out to get Ieyasu!

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:53.220
What? That tiger cub, too?

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:55.640
Whoa, you know Sanada?

00:15:55.640 --> 00:15:59.400
Sounds like things're shapin' up
to get interestin' in the middle.

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:03.110
Fine! I'll take yer side!

00:16:03.110 --> 00:16:03.900
Wh-What?

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:06.530
I smell a big war brewin'.

00:16:06.530 --> 00:16:08.450
This'll be my chance to settle things

00:16:08.450 --> 00:16:11.120
with the greatest warrior o'
the warrin' states in the west.

00:16:11.120 --> 00:16:14.540
We'll fight fer who gets
to be the Ogre after the war!

00:16:17.290 --> 00:16:21.420
You sure are one energetic old geezer.

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:22.040
Bungo

00:16:21.420 --> 00:16:22.420
<i>In the meantime,</i>

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:27.170
<i>Otomo Sorin, who boasts great power in Kyushu,
saw flocking to him many believers of Xavianity,</i>

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:31.390
<i>a mysterious religion that had
swept across the land of the rising sun.</i>

00:16:31.390 --> 00:16:35.220
Lord Mori, we appreciate you
taking the trouble to come all this...

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:38.940
Ah! I have longed to meet you, Tactician!

00:16:38.940 --> 00:16:40.480
No... Sunday!

00:16:40.480 --> 00:16:42.860
T-Tac...? Sunday?

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:45.650
It cannot be! Amnesia?!

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:49.450
What an unfortunate and dramatic turn of events!

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:51.410
Of what do you speak?

00:16:51.410 --> 00:16:54.990
Could this possibly be Lord Xavi testing me?

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:59.460
You are telling me that this time,
I must bring Sunday into the fold myself!

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:01.920
Oh!

00:17:01.920 --> 00:17:07.170
With Lord Xavi in the center...
Sunday! Chest! Joshy!

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:09.550
And me!

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:13.800
Oh, how dreamy!

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:15.720
Oh!

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:18.850
Lord Xavi!

00:17:15.810 --> 00:17:18.060
Otomo          Sorin

00:17:15.810 --> 00:17:18.060
Otomo          Sorin

00:17:20.190 --> 00:17:24.820
<i>Oh, this guy is totally looking
at us like we're crazy.</i>

00:17:24.820 --> 00:17:26.440
We are done talking.

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:30.200
My heart is passionately
urging me not to stay too long.

00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:31.280
I am leaving.

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:36.620
Just watch, I will overcome this test!

00:17:36.620 --> 00:17:39.450
<i>Having left Satsuma,</i>

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:43.000
<i>Chosokabe Motochika moved
on to go see Kuroda Kanbei.</i>

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:44.380
Ishigakibaru

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:46.590
I'll get straight to the point.

00:17:46.590 --> 00:17:50.260
Kuroda Kanbei, won't you
side with Ishida Mitsunari?

00:17:50.260 --> 00:17:51.510
Ishida, you say?

00:17:51.510 --> 00:17:53.680
Yeah, this comes from Otani, too.

00:17:53.680 --> 00:17:57.890
Mitsunari... Gyobu...

00:17:57.890 --> 00:17:59.270
Hell no!

00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:00.890
Kuroda             Kanbei

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:03.020
A request coming from the bastards

00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:04.600
who stuffed my humble self into this hole?

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:06.440
I'll never do it!

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:09.940
Hey, now, I didn't hear about any of this.

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:13.410
I got saddled with one hell of a mess here.

00:18:13.410 --> 00:18:14.950
Take a look at this damn thing!

00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:16.450
Ever since this got put on,

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:19.540
my humble self's luck has
only gotten worse and worse!

00:18:19.540 --> 00:18:20.790
I may not look it, but back in the day,

00:18:20.790 --> 00:18:24.330
I was hailed as the clever one of
Toyotomi's two strategists, you know!

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:27.590
But that Gyobu bastard got jealous and...

00:18:27.590 --> 00:18:31.170
Anyway, I refuse to do anything they want!

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:33.260
If you want to ask my humble self for something,

00:18:33.260 --> 00:18:36.220
bring the damn key to these shackles!

00:18:36.220 --> 00:18:38.890
The key? Does Otani have it?

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:42.230
Gyobu told me that he dropped it during battle!

00:18:42.230 --> 00:18:43.390
What the hell is with that?!

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:46.440
Be more responsible
keeping track of the damn thing!

00:18:46.440 --> 00:18:48.690
Sounds like you've been through a lot, too.

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:50.480
You understand?

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:52.490
You're a good guy!

00:18:52.490 --> 00:18:53.900
Ooh, I have an idea!

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:56.700
I know someone that might
be able to find where the key is!

00:18:56.700 --> 00:18:58.700
What? Who's that?!

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:01.040
It's a little missy who's good at divinations.

00:19:01.040 --> 00:19:04.790
If you hang with me, I bet
<i>she'll</i> be the one to come find <i>us</i>.

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:05.870
How about it?

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:08.590
Join forces with me to get your clue!

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:11.460
Those bastards rub me the wrong way, but...

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:14.170
This'll be for the key to these shackles!

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:17.470
All right! I'll join you!

00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:19.180
Sunpu Castle

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:22.060
I take it that your coming here

00:19:22.060 --> 00:19:24.230
means that you have
decided to become allies with me,

00:19:24.230 --> 00:19:25.810
One-Eyed Dragon?

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:27.440
I've got no such plans.

00:19:27.440 --> 00:19:29.440
I'm gonna crush you

00:19:29.440 --> 00:19:32.190
and make it so Ishida only sees me.

00:19:33.030 --> 00:19:34.990
I won't let anyone interfere!

00:19:34.990 --> 00:19:37.610
Let's go at it one-on-one!

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:39.070
Very well.

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:40.530
You stay put, too, Tadakatsu.

00:19:44.540 --> 00:19:45.710
Draw!

00:19:45.710 --> 00:19:47.370
I have these!

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:51.090
With these fists, I will forge
a bond with you as well!

00:19:51.090 --> 00:19:52.800
You don't wanna mess with me!

00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:55.170
One-Eyed Dragon, I would have
liked to join forces with the old you,

00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:59.010
the straight-as-an-arrow, slightly
cynical guy with his sights set high.

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:01.220
The Dragon fell to the earth!

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:03.720
What can a dragon do,
crawling around on the ground?

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:05.680
I've changed.

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:08.190
I can't go on living if I don't change!

00:20:08.190 --> 00:20:11.110
Then, will you not make a
wager with me on this fight?

00:20:11.110 --> 00:20:12.190
A wager?

00:20:12.190 --> 00:20:16.440
If I win, I want you to change once more!

00:20:16.440 --> 00:20:18.110
I don't care!

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:20.490
I'm never losing again!

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:26.160
What is the matter, One-Eyed Dragon?

00:20:26.160 --> 00:20:28.170
Your movements have no bite to them!

00:20:30.380 --> 00:20:32.090
Shut up!

00:20:37.760 --> 00:20:39.130
Wha...?!

00:20:44.890 --> 00:20:47.430
I win.

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:49.520
Not yet!

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:03.200
Will you still continue?

00:21:20.130 --> 00:21:21.470
Bontenmaru!

